|The three main types of Machine Learning|

A. Supervised Learning
The model learns from examples that include the correct answers, called labels.
Examples: fraud classification, customer churn prediction, loan-default prediction.
Remember: data + correct answers.

B. Unsupervised Learning
The model finds patterns or groups in data without being given target labels.
Examples: grouping customers by spending behavior, discovering unusual activity patterns.
Remember: data without supplied answers.

C. Reinforcement Learning
An agent learns by taking actions and receiving rewards or penalties from an environment.
Examples: game-playing agents, robotics, and some sequential decision-making problems.
Remember: actions + rewards + learning.
