Q1. What is Machine Learning?
Machine Learning is a branch of AI in which algorithms learn patterns from data to make predictions or decisions without requiring every rule to be explicitly programmed.
Q2. What is the difference between AI and ML?
AI is the broader field of intelligent systems. ML is one approach within AI that learns patterns from data.
Q3. What is the difference between supervised and unsupervised learning?
Supervised learning uses labeled data to learn a target. Unsupervised learning looks for patterns or groups in data without supplied target labels.
Q4. What is the difference between training and inference?
Training is when a model learns from data. Inference is when the trained model processes new input to produce a prediction or output.
Q5. Is a GenAI chatbot a Machine Learning application?
Yes. Modern GenAI chatbots commonly use deep learning models trained on large amounts of data to generate responses. Additional components, 
such as retrieval systems and tools, can extend their capabilities.
